# Continuum Studio - UI Paradigm Comparison

direction: down

title: |md
  # UI Paradigm Options
  Comparing layouts and flexibility
|

# Paradigm 1: Tiling Widget System
paradigm1: 1. Tiling Widget System {
  style: {
    fill: "#1a1a2e"
    stroke: "#16213e"
  }
  
  desc: |md
    **Like i3/Hyprland for apps**
    - Automatic space allocation
    - Drag to rearrange
    - Split horizontal/vertical
    - Save/load layouts
  |
  
  mockup: Layout {
    style: {
      fill: "#0f0f23"
      stroke: "#3b82f6"
    }
    
    left: Agent Stream {
      style.fill: "#7c3aed"
    }
    
    center: Editor {
      style.fill: "#2563eb"
    }
    
    right: Vertical Split {
      style.fill: "#1e3a5f"
      
      top: Terminal {
        style.fill: "#059669"
      }
      bottom: Dialogs {
        style.fill: "#f59e0b"
      }
    }
    
    left -> center
    center -> right
    right.top -> right.bottom
  }
  
  pros: |md
    **✅ Pros:**
    - Efficient space use
    - Familiar to Linux users
    - Keyboard-driven
  |
  
  cons: |md
    **❌ Cons:**
    - Learning curve
    - Less intuitive
    - Single window only
  |
}

# Paradigm 2: Tab-Based (Notepad++ style)
paradigm2: 2. Tab-Based Pages {
  style: {
    fill: "#1a1a2e"
    stroke: "#16213e"
  }
  
  desc: |md
    **Enhanced tabbed interface**
    - Tabs = different views
    - Not just editors
    - Easy to understand
    - Tab groups/pinning
  |
  
  mockup: Layout {
    style: {
      fill: "#0f0f23"
      stroke: "#3b82f6"
    }
    
    tabs: Tab Bar {
      style.fill: "#1e293b"
      
      tab1: 📝 Editor
      tab2: 🤖 Agent
      tab3: 💬 Dialog
      tab4: ⚙️ Config
    }
    
    content: Active Content {
      style.fill: "#2563eb"
      height: 300
    }
    
    tabs -> content: shows
  }
  
  pros: |md
    **✅ Pros:**
    - Very familiar
    - Simple mental model
    - Easy to implement
  |
  
  cons: |md
    **❌ Cons:**
    - One thing at a time
    - More switching
    - Less overview
  |
}

# Paradigm 3: Hub and Spoke
paradigm3: 3. Hub & Spoke {
  style: {
    fill: "#1a1a2e"
    stroke: "#16213e"
  }
  
  desc: |md
    **Central control, child windows**
    - Main window = command
    - Spawn task windows
    - Can spread across monitors
    - Each window independent
  |
  
  mockup: Layout {
    style: {
      fill: "#0f0f23"
      stroke: "#3b82f6"
    }
    
    hub: Command Hub {
      style.fill: "#f59e0b"
      
      status: Status
      launch: Launchers
      overview: Overview
    }
    
    spoke1: Editor Window {
      style.fill: "#2563eb"
    }
    
    spoke2: Agent Window {
      style.fill: "#7c3aed"
    }
    
    spoke3: Terminal Window {
      style.fill: "#059669"
    }
    
    hub -> spoke1: spawn
    hub -> spoke2: spawn
    hub -> spoke3: spawn
  }
  
  pros: |md
    **✅ Pros:**
    - Multi-monitor native
    - Flexible placement
    - Independent workflows
  |
  
  cons: |md
    **❌ Cons:**
    - Window management
    - More complex state
    - Desktop clutter
  |
}

# Paradigm 4: Overlay Engine
paradigm4: 4. Overlay Engine {
  style: {
    fill: "#1a1a2e"
    stroke: "#16213e"
  }
  
  desc: |md
    **Game-engine approach**
    - Full GPU rendering
    - Complex animations
    - Cross-monitor canvas
    - Floating panels
  |
  
  mockup: Layout {
    style: {
      fill: "#0f0f23"
      stroke: "#3b82f6"
      shadow: true
    }
    
    layer1: DE Layer {
      style.fill: "#0f172a"
      style.opacity: 0.5
    }
    
    layer2: Overlay Canvas {
      style.fill: "transparent"
      style.stroke: "#f59e0b"
      style.stroke-dash: 3
      
      float1: Agent {
        style.fill: "#7c3aed"
        style.opacity: 0.9
      }
      
      float2: Dialog {
        style.fill: "#f59e0b"
        style.opacity: 0.9
      }
      
      float3: Quick Actions {
        style.fill: "#059669"
        style.opacity: 0.9
      }
    }
    
    layer1 -> layer2: overlay
  }
  
  pros: |md
    **✅ Pros:**
    - Ultimate flexibility
    - Rich animations
    - Unique experience
  |
  
  cons: |md
    **❌ Cons:**
    - Complex to build
    - GPU requirements
    - Accessibility issues
  |
}

# Recommendation
recommendation: Recommendation {
  style: {
    fill: "#065f46"
    stroke: "#10b981"
    stroke-width: 3
  }
  
  text: |md
    ## Hybrid Approach
    
    Start with **Tiling Widgets** as core,
    add **Hub & Spoke** for multi-window,
    use **Overlay** for notifications/dialogs.
    
    This gives maximum flexibility without
    committing to one paradigm.
  |
}

